{
  "name": "r9-chain-membership-write-fault-fences-in-memory-and-halts",
  "requires": "r9",
  "kind": "scenario",
  "side": "host",
  "log": "r9-vectors-membership-log",
  "note": "R9.3 (Astation r3 review 1, r4 review 2): the commit of a valid removal fails before the rename (temp fsync of membership.json); the carriage record and the intent are durable. Atem fails closed in the same step, exactly like §H's failed revocation write: the removed principal's attachments are fenced, its lease revoked (its queued raw input is dropped at the write boundary), its accepted work rejected, all in memory; the journal halts, so remote admission, dispatch and remote input stop until the restart; local input goes on. At restart the carriage record is replayed (E7 committed, svc fenced) and, since the halted run wrote no membership checkpoint, the host is held: no remote principal is admitted, not even after another orderly restart and a day, until a managing device whose verified log ends at the host's head reconciles; pre-restart work is rejected (no clean close).",
